@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Reference / reusable template. Illustrative contract/model/pattern, not a product release commitment.
title Template example — Optional concurrency: guarded competing publications
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

participant "Command A (expected v12)" as A
participant "Coordination mechanism" as G
participant "Command B (expected v12)" as B
database "Current draft / revision / pointer / result" as D
A -> G : acquire chosen resource / identity guard
G --> A : admitted
B -> G : competing guard request
G --> B : wait / conflict per actual mechanism
A -> D : current authority + version + identity check
A -> D : coherent commit A
A -> G : release
B -> G : establish current admission
G --> B : admitted when actually eligible
B -> D : reread current state and identity
note over B,D
 A publication need not increment the draft version.
 Distinct explicit commands may both be valid if source policy permits.
 Same command identity must resolve one attributable result.
 Define actual pointer ordering; do not invent a guaranteed loser.
end note

@enduml
